STATEMENT
  HS band at vf = 0.3000: [3696.1, 3766.3] MPa (band width 1.90 % - very narrow, because the equivalent particle is only ~1.3x stiffer than the epoxy).
  FE values span 3794.7-3809.1 MPa, i.e. ALL FOUR lie ABOVE the HS bounds by +0.93 % of the upper bound.
  FE mean is +2.85 % relative to Mori-Tanaka (3696.1 MPa); |rel diff| < 25 %.
  Interpretation of the overshoot (NOT taken as agreement):
    - KUBC is a kinematically constrained (upper-bound-type) estimator: on a finite,
      non-periodic RVE it returns an APPARENT stiffness that exceeds the true effective
      modulus, so it is not required to respect the HS upper bound. Periodic BCs
      (not implemented in foamsim.fem) would bracket it from below.
    - Voxel meshes stiffen curved interfaces; the FE value decreases monotonically with
      resolution (16 -> 24: 3807.1 -> 3795.7 MPa), i.e. it is converging
      downward toward the bound but has not converged at these resolutions.
    - The overshoot (~1 % of E_hi) is the size of these two artefacts, and the HS band
      here is only ~2 % wide, so this is a resolution/BC bias, not a constitutive error;
      the homogeneous-box check in step 0 was exact to 1e-16, which rules out an
      assembly/BC implementation bug.
    - To confirm rather than assume: rerun with larger n and more spheres/seeds and
      check that E_FE continues to fall toward the HS band.
  The 2-seed / 2-resolution spread quoted above is numerical uncertainty, not physical scatter.
